          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What the independent tests say</h3>

          <p>
            Neither of the two big recent studies covers Ora. Consumer Reports' October 2025 investigation tested 23 protein powders and shakes; Ora was not among them, according to the full list published by NBC News. Plant-based products averaged about nine times the lead of dairy products in that test, and the two organic plant proteins we compare below, Garden of Life Sport and Orgain, landed in the limit-weekly and occasional-use groups. The Clean Label Project's 2025 report, which found that about 77% of plant-based powders it tested exceeded Prop 65 lead limits, did not name brands at all.
